# of_len_zero_fill.tkr — the COL-F0a anchor-form fixture (crumb 0021). `main.tks` allocates a
# fixed `[]i64` of `cfg::SLOTS` slots via `teko::list::of_len<i64>(n)`, asserts every slot came
# back zero (the one memset-zero pass), then writes each position by index under a `count`
# watermark and reads them back — proving the array is FIXED (`xs.len == n`, never grown) and that
# index-assign + `count` is the presence idiom. It exits 0 only if the zero-fill, the watermark
# count, the fixed length and the written sum all hold. The self-build never allocates a fixed
# VALUE array through the named builtin yet, so this path is not fixpoint-exercised. Pinned to the
# C backend: `of_len` lowers on the C route and the native leg honest-stops (N2).

Feature: of_len_zero_fill — of_len<i64>(n) is a fixed, zero-filled backing written by index

  Scenario: of_len_returns_n_zeroed_slots_written_by_index_under_a_count_watermark
    Given env = ["TEKO_BACKEND=c"]
    When the program is built and run
    Then it exits 0
